# Virus reactivation in acute and long COVID-19 

---
Contact Information: Cole Maguire (colemag@utexas.edu)
## Instructions
This code is for the manuscript titled "Chronic Viral Reactivation and Associated Host Immune Response and Clinical Outcomes in Acute COVID-19 and Post-Acute Sequelae of COVID-19"
Update 6/16/2025: The codebase has been updated for revisions to the manuscript as part of the peer review process. Due to Figures shifting, particularly the supplement, a mapping of the pre-print supplement to the current supplement is provided at the bottom.
Update 5/3/2026: The codebase has been updated to match the final figure order. Of note, Extended Data Figures are still referred to as "Supplementary Figures" and are denoted with an "S" in front of them (e.g. Figure S2A would be Extended Data Figure 2a). The mapping of figures compared to the pre-print has been updated at the bottom of this file. The data availability statement has been updated to include more details.
### Data availability
The IMPACC Data Sharing Plan aims to support broad data dissemination while safeguarding participant privacy and data integrity through de-identification and masking of sensitive data fields. All IMPACC data, including those produced as part of this study, have been submitted to the Immunology Database and Analysis Portal (ImmPort), a repository supported by the NIAID Division of Allergy, Immunology and Transplantation under accession code SDY1760 (https://www.immport.org/shared/study/SDY1760), as well as to the NLM's Database of Genotypes and Phenotypes (dbGaP) under accession number phs002686.v2.p2. Both raw and processed datasets are available through restricted access in accordance with the NIH public data sharing policy for IRB-exempted public health surveillance studies. Access may be requested through AccessClinicalData@NIAID (https://accessclinicaldata.niaid.nih.gov/study-viewer/clinical_trials). Further detailed guidance on data access is provided on ImmPort (https://docs.immport.org/home/impaccslides).
Once downloaded, see the [data_object_generation.Rmd](data_object_generation.qmd) file for how to load the omics into a singular data environment (which downstream Figure code will depend on).

### Code Install and Run Time
The codebase itself is small and should install in a few minutes or less depending on your download speed. The run time is variable between the figures' scripts, the GAMM modeling may take much longer to run than other files.

